<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Davenport</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1597–1670</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Davenport was an English Puritan minister who left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a> in 1637 and in 1638 founded the New Haven Colony with the merchant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theophilus-eaton">Theophilus Eaton</a>. He shaped its strict church-based government, in which only church members could vote. He opposed the colony's absorption into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a> in 1665 and later moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a>, where he died.</p></div>
